# HTCondor submit file — the seed-1 control for the final AL benchmark run (2026-11-09).
#
# The second-seed encoders of the final run (epochs 21 and 26 of the preset
# full_sp_50ep_seed1) start from another initialisation than the random-init control of
# that run (chemprop_untrained, seed 0), so their gain over random initialisation mixes the
# effect of training with the difference between two initialisations. This run adds the
# missing control: the untrained starting point of the seed-1 run (its epoch_000.pt, saved
# before the first update), benchmarked exactly like every other representation.
#
#   seed1_control   4 jobs, one per target, representation chemprop_untrained_seed1;
#                   TabPFN, RF, RBF GP and Tanimoto GP; greedy, EI and PI at y+ and
#                   y_thresh, for TabPFN from the Gaussian form AND the bar distribution;
#                   4 budget configurations x 5 seeds; 1,000 candidates per round. The same
#                   arms as the seed-1 encoders of `final`.
#   repro_check     1 job: the final run's D2R / Morgan job, rerun under another name.
#                   Morgan is computed on the CPU and reproduced bit for bit between earlier
#                   runs, so the output must equal final_d2r_morgan.csv in every column
#                   except `experiment` and `seconds`. If it does, these later jobs ran the
#                   code and environment of the final run, and seed1_control can be paired
#                   with it. If it does not, do not pair seed1_control with `final`.
#
# Expected cost (round time of the same arms in the final run): seed1_control 3.0 h
# (TYK2), 2.9 h (S. aureus), 2.2 h (USP7) and 1.7 h (D2R); repro_check 5.2 h. About
# 15 GPU-hours in all; with five free GPUs the wall time is set by repro_check, about 5-6 h.
#
# Outputs, per seed and per round, in experiments/benchmark_final/:
#   seed1_control_<target>_chemprop_untrained_seed1.csv   and   repro_check_d2r_morgan.csv
# Neither name matches "final_*.csv", so the analyses of the final run (plot_benchmark.py)
# do not pick them up; seed1_control is a separate control, not part of the benchmark grid.
# A requeued job RESUMES its file (finished campaigns kept, a cut-off one re-run), so never
# submit this file twice while jobs from it are still queued or running.
#
# BEFORE SUBMITTING, on the cluster:
#   1. the updated src/scripts/benchmark_extended.py must be there (it defines both
#      experiments); commit it first, so that the run is tied to a recorded version;
#   2. experiments/trained_encoder_full_sp_50ep_seed1_epochs/epoch_000.pt must exist
#      (the final run read epochs 21 and 26 from the same folder);
#   3. experiments/benchmark_final/ must not already hold seed1_control_* or
#      repro_check_* files from a test run (they would be resumed, not rerun).
#
# Submit from the repo root, after `mkdir -p runlogs`:
#   condor_submit -dry-run /dev/null cluster/run_gpu_benchmark_final_seed1_control.sub   # validate only
#   condor_submit cluster/run_gpu_benchmark_final_seed1_control.sub
universe                = docker
docker_image            = pytorch/pytorch:2.3.1-cuda12.1-cudnn8-devel
executable              = cluster/run_gpu_benchmark_extended.sh
arguments               = $(EXPERIMENT) $(TARGET) $(REPRESENTATION)
output                  = runlogs/run_gpu_benchmark_final_seed1_control_$(EXPERIMENT)_$(TARGET)_$(REPRESENTATION).$(ClusterId).out
error                   = runlogs/run_gpu_benchmark_final_seed1_control_$(EXPERIMENT)_$(TARGET)_$(REPRESENTATION).$(ClusterId).err
log                     = runlogs/run_gpu_benchmark_final_seed1_control.$(ClusterId).log

should_transfer_files   = YES
when_to_transfer_output = ON_EXIT
getenv                  = HOME

request_GPUs            = 1
request_CPUs            = 4
request_memory          = 7GB
require_gpus            = (GlobalMemoryMb >= 40000)
requirements            = UidDomain == "cs.uni-saarland.de"
+WantGPUHomeMounted     = true
+WantScratchMounted     = true

queue EXPERIMENT, TARGET, REPRESENTATION from (
    repro_check,   d2r,     morgan
    seed1_control, tyk2,    chemprop_untrained_seed1
    seed1_control, saureus, chemprop_untrained_seed1
    seed1_control, usp7,    chemprop_untrained_seed1
    seed1_control, d2r,     chemprop_untrained_seed1
)
